    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` pipeline now emits an audit line on successful create.\n\n**Changes (2 files, low structural impact):**\n\n1. **New function class** `AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 a single small, cohesive step (WMC_other = 0) that logs via the `AUDIT` logger:\n   ```java\n   AUDIT.info(\"Owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n       owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n   ```\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted an `audit` step between `save` and `respond`, so it runs after the id is assigned but before the response is sent, under the same transaction governance.\n\nI deliberately added a new step rather than editing `SaveOwner` or `RespondWithOwnerCreated`, keeping every existing function untouched \u2014 no method grew and no large class absorbed the change. `LocalDate.toString()` yields ISO `yyyy-MM-dd`, which matches the JSON `registrationDate` the test asserts against, and the emitted line (`AUDIT - Owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-03`) carries all three required values.",
